HST Office: print scaling in Sheets moves from the Sheet tab to the Page tab, as in Excel.

- ScPageScalePage hosts SvxPageDescPage (shared with Writer and Slides, in libcui) below the scaling controls and hands it
  every tab-page duty, so that page and its .ui stay as they are for the other two applications.
- The scale code moves unchanged from ScTablePage and uses the same items, so values in existing files keep working.
  One upstream slip is fixed on the way: a changed "height in pages" compared the width with the old height.
- The strings keep their sheetprintpage contexts, so the translations stay.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-sheets.py page-setup.
